From: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: emc2305: preserve initial fan duty at probe

With thermal support enabled, probe writes the minimum duty to each
fan even when no cooling map or userspace fan controller is configured.
The default minimum is zero, stopping the fan when the driver binds.

Read the existing duty before registering the cooling device and retain
it unless registration applies a thermal state. In common-channel mode,
retain the highest initial duty among the fans, clamped to the configured
minimum. This preserves reset/firmware cooling instead of dropping it
when this driver becomes built in on NMS-SM-K1892VM21YA.

Signed-off-by: INMYS <support@inmys.ru>
---
--- a/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
@@ -307,6 +307,14 @@
 
 	cdev_idx = (idx) ? idx - 1 : 0;
 	pwm = data->pwm_min[cdev_idx];
+	/* Preserve firmware/reset cooling instead of stopping fans at probe. */
+	for (i = data->pwm_separate ? cdev_idx : 0;
+	     i < (data->pwm_separate ? cdev_idx + 1 : data->pwm_num); i++) {
+		ret = emc2305_show_pwm(dev, i);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+		pwm = max_t(long, pwm, ret);
+	}
 
 	data->cdev_data[cdev_idx].cdev =
 		devm_thermal_of_cooling_device_register(dev, fan_node,
@@ -323,7 +331,7 @@
 		pwm = EMC2305_PWM_STATE2DUTY(data->cdev_data[cdev_idx].cur_state,
 					     data->max_state, EMC2305_FAN_MAX);
 
-	/* Set minimal PWM speed. */
+	/* Retain the initial duty unless a thermal policy has selected one. */
 	if (data->pwm_separate) {
 		ret = emc2305_set_pwm(dev, pwm, cdev_idx);
 		if (ret < 0)
